<main id="main"><section class="pageHero compact"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Legal</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: 23 August 2026</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container legalProse"><h2>What we collect</h2><p>When you contact us or submit an order request we may collect your name, email address, company, country, requested service, order requirements and correspondence. If you become a customer, we may also process billing, account, service, network and support information needed to provide the service and meet legal obligations.</p><h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use personal information to respond to enquiries, assess and fulfil orders, provide support, protect services from abuse and fraud, maintain records, comply with legal obligations and communicate material service information.</p><h2>Infrastructure providers</h2><p>Service delivery may require limited information to be processed by datacentre, hosting, connectivity, payment, email or other service providers. We seek to share only information reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose.</p><h2>Retention</h2><p>Enquiry and account information is kept only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose collected, legal obligations, security, dispute handling and accounting requirements.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on applicable law, you may have rights to access, correct, erase, restrict or object to processing of your personal data. Contact <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.privacy %>"><%= site.emails.privacy %></a> to make a privacy request.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect information. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p><h2>Website tracking</h2><p>This website is designed to operate without advertising trackers or analytics cookies by default. See our Cookie Policy for more information.</p></div></section></main>
